{{ if eq (.profile | lower) "mac" -}}
# Host {{ .chezmoi.hostname }} (macOS) — runtimes, packages
{{- else -}}
# Host {{ .chezmoi.hostname }} (Arch {{ if eq (.profile | lower) "omarchy" }}desktop{{ else }}server{{ end }}) — runtimes, packages, sudo
{{- end }}

- Runtimes via mise (`mise use -g <tool>`): node, python, uv, on-demand pnpm/bun.
  Neovim via bob. NEVER install node tooling or editors via {{ if eq (.profile | lower) "mac" }}homebrew — homebrew's{{ else }}pacman — pacman's{{ end }}
  node/npm/pnpm/bun/neovim/vim were deliberately removed. (claude-code is a native
  install, not the {{ if eq (.profile | lower) "mac" }}homebrew{{ else }}pacman{{ end }} package.)
{{ if eq (.profile | lower) "mac" -}}
- Packages are tracked under `packages/mac/`; reconciliation is an explicit reviewed command.
{{- else -}}
{{- if eq (.profile | lower) "server" -}}
- Packages never sync or remove themselves. Regenerate deliberately with
  `~/.local/share/chezmoi/scripts/update_server_package_lists.sh`,
  review the diff, and run `scripts/reconcile-packages.sh --check` before reconciliation.
{{- else -}}
- Omarchy package lists in `~/.local/share/chezmoi/packages/omarchy/` are hand-edited.
  `czu` runs `scripts/update_package_lists.sh` (interactive, needs a TTY) to record drift;
  run `scripts/reconcile-packages.sh --check` before a manual reconciliation.
{{- end }}
- Avoid commands that trigger interactive `sudo` prompts unless asked.
{{- end }}
